    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cambridge was chartered in August 1781 and first settled in 1783 by John Safford from New Hampshire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Cambridge suggests the University of Cambridge in England, as the land was originally reserved for a university.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cambridge and neighboring Johnson were once known as the King's College Tract, created by authority of King George III in 1764.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Lamoille River flows across the center of Cambridge, providing water power for the town's early watermills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early industries in Cambridge included a woolen factory, a tannery, a gristmill, and several sawmills and cabinet shops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
